Chattha Saṅgāyana (VRI) edition anusauraṇena, imaṃ udāharaṇaṃ (Dhammapada 15) evameva paripūrehi:

"Asso yathā bhadro kasāniviṭṭho, ātāpino saṃvegino bhavātha;
Saddhāya sīlena ca **paññāya, tathā vutthāyāyamehi.**"

Chattha Saṅgāyana (VRI) edition-athena imaṃ udāharaṇaṃ paripūrehi:

"Kāyena saṃvaro sādhu, sādhu vācāya saṃvaro;
Manasā saṃvaro **sādhu**."

The completion of the verse from the **Chattha Saṅgāyana (VRI)** edition is as follows:

"Duppabbajjaṃ durabhiramaṃ, durāvāsā gharā dukhā;
Dukkhosamānasaṃvāso, dukkhānupatitaddhagū;
Tasmā **vissajjehi gharāni, anupahāreṇa dūrehi.**"

***

**Full Verse (Pāli):**
> Duppabbajjaṃ durabhiramaṃ, durāvāsā gharā dukhā;
> Dukkhosamānasaṃvāso, dukkhānupatitaddhagū;
> Tasmā vissajjehi gharāni, anupahāreṇa dūrehi.

**Translation (General Meaning):**
"The home-life is difficult to leave, difficult to find pleasure in, and difficult to dwell in; it is full of sorrow. Living together with a spouse is painful, and the clinging to the household is painful. Therefore, abandon the home-life and go far away, without any attachments."
